        "body": "This release is about speed! The build is faster, the `build_data` script is faster, the MSA featurisation is 10x faster, and – most importantly – Jackhmmer search is ~2.5x faster and now nicely scales with `--jackhmmer_n_cpu`. On a machine with 24 cores, we saw >10x speedup of Jackhmmer runs! There is also a lot of small bug fixes, documentation improvements and better error messages – thanks to the community for reporting/suggesting many of these.\r\n\r\n### Change log\r\nFull change log: [v3.0.4...v3.0.5](https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphafold3/compare/v3.0.4...v3.0.5.)\r\n\r\n### New features\r\n\r\n* You can now configure the number of CPUs that Hmmsearch uses using the `--hmmsearch_n_cpu` flag. Thanks @Ayush7614.\r\n* Added a parallel `shard_databases.sh` helper script.\r\n* Majority of AlphaFold 3 unit tests are now included in the repo and run in CI.\r\n\r\n### Performance improvements\r\n\r\n* Added compilation buckets of size 128 and 384 to make running small proteins faster by default. Thanks @teerthsharma.\r\n* Sped up MSA featurisation ~10x.\r\n* The CCD is now stored using MessagePack instead of pickle, which makes build_data 5x faster.\r\n* Sped up the build by about 1.5x (120 -> 85 s).\r\n* Sped up the build_data script by about 10 s by using MessagePack instead of pickle to store the processed CCD.\r\n* Made Jackhmmer ~2.5x faster + made it scale with the number of CPUs. On a test 24-core machine it runs >10x faster!\r\n* Multiple Structure class performance improvements, mainly around filtering. Thanks @akviz!\r\n\r\n### Bug fixes\r\n\r\n* Fix loading of a template with empty mapping written by AlphaFold prior to 3.0.4. Thanks @mooreneural.\r\n* Don't leak resources when sharded Jackhmmer/Nhmmer errors out. Thanks @Ayush7614.\r\n* Use the original RNA sequence (not the modified one) in `RnaChain.fill_missing_fields()`. Thanks @Ayush7614.\r\n* Prevent mutation of the cached base CCD dictionary when applying user CCD. Thanks @cindykrafft.\r\n* Avoid float32 overflow when ranking paired MSA rows. Thanks @shubhxho.\r\n* Reject mixed-case and non-ASCII chain IDs at input validation. Thanks @harshitgavita-07.\r\n* Preserve chain order stable across a to_json / from_json round trip. Thanks @cindykrafft.\r\n* Fix chain_ids in the summary confidences JSON to be one entry per chain. Thanks @cindykrafft.\r\n* Fix check that exactly one of `--json_path` or `--input_dir` is set. Thanks @romainhedouin.\r\n* Improved input validation. Thanks @Nas01010101.\r\n* The MSA hit order is preserved when pairing by species. Thanks @YMuskrat.\r\n\r\n### Documentation\r\n\r\n* Better error when third party tools can't be find on PATH. Thanks @Ayush7614.\r\n* More detailed documentation of the effect of the JAX compilation cache. Thanks @mooreneural.\r\n* Better documentation for the Nhmmer Z-value. Thanks @cindykrafft.\r\n* Document that linked ketoses keep their leaving atom. Thanks @shahriararab and @sridhar-3009.\r\n\r\nWe thank the following people for their pull requests and/or great suggestions: @akviz, @Ayush7614, @cindykrafft, @harshitgavita-07, @mooreneural, @Nas01010101, @shahriararab, @shubhxho, @sridhar-3009, @teerthsharma, @YMuskrat.",
